/-- Symmetric Bregman lower bounds imply gradient strong monotonicity.

For a carrier `P` evaluated in a real inner-product space, if the two directed
Bregman terms each dominate half of the squared seminorm displacement and their
sum is the usual gradient-difference pairing, then the selected gradient is
strongly monotone in that seminorm.

