  monotonicity before mirror-prox stability estimates
Book citation: book/FOML/StochasticBlockMirrorDescent.json#/algorithm_spec
Origin algorithm: Lan, First-order and Stochastic Optimization Methods for
  Machine Learning, stochastic block mirror descent -/
theorem bregman_gradient_strong_mono_of_symmetric_lower_bound
    {P E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    (V : P → P → ℝ) (eval grad : P → E) (p : Seminorm ℝ E) (x y : P)
    (hxy : (1 / 2 : ℝ) * p (eval x - eval y) ^ 2 ≤ V y x)
    (hyx : (1 / 2 : ℝ) * p (eval y - eval x) ^ 2 ≤ V x y)
    (hsymm : V y x + V x y = ⟪grad x - grad y, eval x - eval y⟫_ℝ) :
    p (eval x - eval y) ^ 2 ≤
      ⟪grad x - grad y, eval x - eval y⟫_ℝ := by
  have hpnorm :
      p (eval y - eval x) = p (eval x - eval y) := by
    have hsub : eval y - eval x = -(eval x - eval y) := by
      abel
    rw [hsub]
    simpa using map_neg_eq_map p (eval x - eval y)
  have hyx' : (1 / 2 : ℝ) * p (eval x - eval y) ^ 2 ≤ V x y := by
    simpa [hpnorm] using hyx
  nlinarith [hxy, hyx', hsymm]

