carrier `S`, the map `(x, z) ↦ v x - v z - ⟪grad z, eval x - eval z⟫` is
continuous on `S × S`.

Layer: Model | Gap: Level 1 (carrier-product Bregman formula continuity)
Proof: compose the potential, gradient selector, and evaluation maps with the
  two product projections using the `ContinuousOn.comp` maps-to side
  conditions, then combine subtraction and inner-product continuity.
Source: Mathlib product topology, setwise continuity, and real inner-product
  continuity APIs
Used in: stochastic accelerated primal-dual and mirror-descent prox-selector
  continuity for Bregman kernels
Book citation: book/FOML/StochasticAcceleratedPrimalDual.json#/algorithm_spec
Origin algorithm: Lan, First-order and Stochastic Optimization Methods for
  Machine Learning, stochastic accelerated primal-dual -/
theorem continuousOn_bregmanFormula_of_continuousOn
    {P E : Type*} [TopologicalSpace P] [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    {S : Set P} {v : P → ℝ} {grad : P → E} {eval : P → E}
    (hv : ContinuousOn v S) (hgrad : ContinuousOn grad S) (heval : ContinuousOn eval S) :
    ContinuousOn (fun p : P × P => carrierBregmanFormula v eval grad p.2 p.1)
      (S ×ˢ S) := by
  have hpot_left : ContinuousOn (fun p : P × P => v p.1) (S ×ˢ S) :=
    hv.comp continuous_fst.continuousOn (by
      intro p hp
      exact hp.1)
  have hpot_right : ContinuousOn (fun p : P × P => v p.2) (S ×ˢ S) :=
    hv.comp continuous_snd.continuousOn (by
      intro p hp
      exact hp.2)
  have hgrad_right : ContinuousOn (fun p : P × P => grad p.2) (S ×ˢ S) :=
    hgrad.comp continuous_snd.continuousOn (by
      intro p hp
      exact hp.2)
  have heval_left : ContinuousOn (fun p : P × P => eval p.1) (S ×ˢ S) :=
    heval.comp continuous_fst.continuousOn (by
      intro p hp
      exact hp.1)
  have heval_right : ContinuousOn (fun p : P × P => eval p.2) (S ×ˢ S) :=
    heval.comp continuous_snd.continuousOn (by
      intro p hp
      exact hp.2)
  have hinner :
      ContinuousOn (fun p : P × P => ⟪grad p.2, eval p.1 - eval p.2⟫_ℝ) (S ×ˢ S) :=
    hgrad_right.inner (heval_left.sub heval_right)
  simpa [carrierBregmanFormula] using (hpot_left.sub hpot_right).sub hinner

