/-- Declared squared-radius bound for a Bregman kernel on feasible pairs.

`bregmanDiameterBound V X D` is the source-assumption form used in many
mirror and primal-dual algorithms: every ordered pair of feasible points has
Bregman value at most `D ^ 2`.

