If `v` is `m`-strongly convex on a carrier `X` and `grad a` is a genuine
ambient gradient of `v` at the feasible base point `a`, then the carrier
Bregman formula at any feasible endpoint `b` dominates `m / 2` times the
squared Hilbert distance.

